{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787876733633177001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"rubied-nonvagrant-whimbrel","assignee":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":8,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"eb5a0affea6aff85061de03328cd744b2df8860a65882be16b83db90c50f658a","event_uuid":"90fbc7fe-600e-4a48-843a-812d90459e40","position":{"commit_sha":"e0de9ca9b394a9e3aa55c94d81570c82371bd796","position":"1787868647534036001-90fbc7fe-600e-4a48-843a-812d90459e40"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"08afb0e5d1b3ea4dec4b27e60932d7161bee47f6cc404ebd95f577b698328412","event_uuid":"6bafa874-2df5-4364-9447-07bf7b81cf3b","position":{"commit_sha":"0883073408a8ff5598c374a3ea076c8ec8440f0b","position":"1787869396554002001-6bafa874-2df5-4364-9447-07bf7b81cf3b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a8991884e784450baf325f7b18082080fb2f126bbdac62532cb8e9d11ffb5dea","event_uuid":"4bb6799c-eb95-4b61-ad86-722956cee692","position":{"commit_sha":"ddd13500ffbbf5547283692a8e62a2906e406f45","position":"1787869707178505175-4bb6799c-eb95-4b61-ad86-722956cee692"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e2405975ff10f393d58b1b4360571da47762dad0ef8d1a72cae58361ec373590","event_uuid":"c642b9a0-6dd5-43b3-abef-7c8a7e3e7cc5","position":{"commit_sha":"ddd13500ffbbf5547283692a8e62a2906e406f45","position":"1787869707226616989-c642b9a0-6dd5-43b3-abef-7c8a7e3e7cc5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"1fc32b42fd701d808c8461f64709c558a8c06c9f8bd1b70be1297ff52acb9d59","event_uuid":"fb7ed8d1-dd42-46d1-b41f-08c9320dffd8","position":{"commit_sha":"421187fc0aa3e9a7509043a97495b7ebd39145f4","position":"1787869828054668681-fb7ed8d1-dd42-46d1-b41f-08c9320dffd8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"3c359611802bc58dde29ed56e22f1ecc933ec0a6236853da6613c07e4bf3f979","event_uuid":"75bd17cd-cd99-4a59-a412-010e6a26e967","position":{"commit_sha":"a3379794c9d2724a1e895fe91efc18b971af2e4f","position":"1787869863485307867-75bd17cd-cd99-4a59-a412-010e6a26e967"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"5e8588a54e8665544a7d8345e28fe8025afda50e18ad1930aea646062ae27b94","event_uuid":"61042ec2-bb89-426c-a84f-78f02d5bfce7","position":{"commit_sha":"be15e4ad2b1f082a78ea6fb78842d9d0a8f9ac8d","position":"1787869897432721299-61042ec2-bb89-426c-a84f-78f02d5bfce7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"b54b61e1e99753b66ec5ac6c81a1b147a7e223288a2863d9971e18fa68d22733","event_uuid":"900e372a-18cb-4b08-b7ed-82d45ce3f09f","position":{"commit_sha":"acbe58e90020eefee087cfc143d028d3e0abb90b","position":"1787869958395978001-900e372a-18cb-4b08-b7ed-82d45ce3f09f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## RCA — confirmed root cause (Phase 1 complete)\n\n### Mechanism\n\n`templatefile()` interpolates the **entire** file as an HCL template. Shell comment syntax is\ninvisible to it: a `#` line is template text like any other. `$${` is the escape for a literal\n`${`; an unescaped `${name}` is an interpolation whose `name` must resolve against the template\nvariable map.\n\n`infra/terraform/main.tf:63` declares exactly **one** variable:\n\n    user_data = templatefile(\"${path.module}/user_data.sh\", {\n      data_volume_id = aws_ebs_volume.data.id\n    })\n\nA scan of `user_data.sh` (proper escape-aware scanner, not a naive grep — it consumes `$$`/`%%`\nas escapes) finds **7** unescaped interpolation sequences, split cleanly in two:\n\n**Legitimate (4)** — all reference the declared `data_volume_id`, all must stay unescaped:\n\n- `:25:42`, `:28:20`, `:53:57`, `:56:28`\n\n**Broken (3)** — reference `PARAMS`, a *bash* associative array that is not a template variable:\n\n- `:92:14`  — `# reduces to ${!PARAMS[@]} / ...`\n- `:92:30`  — `# ... / ${PARAMS[$name]}. ...`\n- `:111:46` — `# After rendering, \"$${!PARAMS[@]}\" becomes \"${!PARAMS[@]}\" ...`\n\nAll three are inside `#` comments, and each escapes the *first* mention (`$${...}`) while leaving\nthe \"reduces to\" / \"becomes\" half unescaped. Terraform then tries to parse `!PARAMS[@]` as an HCL\nexpression — hence `Invalid character; This character is not used within the language` at the `!`.\n\n### Discriminating experiment\n\nIsolated the template evaluation from the rest of the config in `/tmp/tfprobe` (a one-output\n`.tf` calling `templatefile()` on a copy of the file, so nothing but the template is under test):\n\n1. **RED** — unmodified copy reproduces the report verbatim:\n\n       Call to function \"templatefile\" failed: ./user_data.sh:92,24-25: Invalid\n       character; This character is not used within the language., and 3 other\n       diagnostic(s).\n\n2. **GREEN** — escaping *only* those 3 sites (leaving all 4 `data_volume_id` sites untouched)\n   renders the whole file successfully; the plan completes and emits the rendered script.\n\nThat splits the account cleanly: the 3 comment sites are **necessary and sufficient**. It also\nrules out the rival hypothesis \"any `${` in the file breaks it\" — the 4 `data_volume_id` sites are\nunescaped and entirely fine, which is exactly why the regression guard must be\n**declared-variable-aware** rather than a blanket ban on `${`.\n\nIndependently confirmed `terraform init` succeeds and the S3 backend is reachable (the failing run\nacquired and released a real state lock), so remote state is not implicated.\n\n### Defect origin\n\n**`fe4e-54a5-3c3a-4901`** — commit `ef1a7e66a65d` \"Gate standalone shell scripts with ShellCheck\".\n\n`git blame -w -C -M` on the implicated lines attributes 91, 92, 93 and 111 to that commit\n(2026-08-26). Line 90 predates it (`30c92d4f43df`, 2026-06-29) and is *correctly* escaped — the\ncarrier check therefore stops at `ef1a7e66a65d` rather than walking further back. Date test passes:\nthe implicated lines are the same age as the good→bad transition, so this is a genuine\n**regression**, not an unmet obligation inherited from elsewhere.\n\nThe commit message itself shows the awareness gap:\n\n> terraform/user_data.sh: three justified line-scoped disables. It is a templatefile() source, so\n> ShellCheck lints it pre-render and resolves neither the Terraform interpolation nor the\n> `$${...}` escaping.\n\nThe change correctly identified the file as a `templatefile()` source and correctly escaped the\nprose it *quoted*, then wrote a second, unescaped copy of the same expansion in the explanatory\nhalf of each sentence. A reviewer on that ticket could plausibly have caught it, which is the test\nfor a correct attribution.\n\n### Legitimacy: `defect` (regression)\n\nAuthoritative source: `terraform plan` ran green before `ef1a7e66a65d` and fails after, on an\notherwise untouched configuration — an existing behaviour broke. Not a feature request, not\nintended behaviour.\n\n## Fix plan\n\n1. **`infra/terraform/user_data.sh`** — reword the three comment sites so the explanation survives\n   and no unescaped `${` remains. Straight `$$`-escaping of the second half is rejected: it renders\n   both halves identically, turning \"X reduces to X\" into nonsense in the file that actually lands\n   on the box. Instead state the *rule* (and the trap that caused this bug) rather than printing\n   the post-render form a second time.\n\n2. **`scripts/check_templatefile_escapes.py`** (new) — the regression guard. ShellCheck cannot\n   catch this class: the file is valid bash and the breakage is in a different consumer. The guard\n   parses `templatefile(...)` call sites out of the `.tf` files, extracts each call's **declared\n   variable names**, escape-aware-scans the referenced template, and fails on any interpolation\n   whose root identifier is not declared. That is the semantically correct rule — it accepts the\n   4 legitimate `data_volume_id` sites and rejects the 3 broken `PARAMS` ones.\n\n3. **`Makefile`** — wire into `lint`, following the existing `scripts/check_*.py` gate pattern.\n\n4. **`tests/unit/test_check_templatefile_escapes.py`** — RED→GREEN→mutation coverage plus the\n   `make lint` wiring assertion the sibling gates use.\n\nBlast radius is local: the comment edit changes only `user_data`, and\n`user_data_replace_on_change` defaults to `false`, so this is an **in-place update** — it does not\nrebuild the Gerrit instance.\n","timestamp":1787869828054668681}],"created_at":1787868647534036001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"61042ec2-bb89-426c-a84f-78f02d5bfce7","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"fe4e-54a5-3c3a-4901"}],"description":"## Summary\n\n`terraform plan` cannot run at all against `infra/terraform`. Every terraform operation on this\nbox is blocked — not just the change that discovered it.\n\n    Error in function call\n      on main.tf line 63: user_data = templatefile(\"${path.module}/user_data.sh\", {...})\n    Call to function \"templatefile\" failed: ./user_data.sh:92,24-25: Invalid character;\n    This character is not used within the language., and 3 other diagnostic(s).\n\n## Root cause\n\nMerged commit `ef1a7e66a65d` (\"Gate standalone shell scripts with ShellCheck\") added explanatory\nCOMMENTS to `infra/terraform/user_data.sh`. Each escapes the FIRST mention of a bash brace\nexpansion as `$${...}` but leaves the 'reduces to' / 'becomes' half UNESCAPED. Three sites, all\ninside `#` comments:\n\n- `:92`  — `# reduces to ${!PARAMS[@]} / ${PARAMS[$name]}. ...`\n- `:111` — `# After rendering, \"$${!PARAMS[@]}\" becomes \"${!PARAMS[@]}\" ...`\n\nHarmless to bash — a comment is a comment. Fatal to `templatefile()`, which interpolates the\nWHOLE file regardless of shell comment syntax and tries to evaluate `${!PARAMS[@]}` as HCL.\n\n## Why this is P1\n\nIt blocks ALL terraform work on this box, not one ticket. `-target` does not help: terraform\nevaluates the entire configuration before honouring `-target`, so a plan restricted to four SSM\nparameters fails identically. There is no narrow path around it.\n\nDiscovered while attempting the `terraform apply` that `colourless-hasteless-lamb` needs. That\nchange (`0f1d0cfc7792`) does NOT touch `user_data.sh` — the file is byte-identical to\n`origin/main`, so this is pre-existing and independent.\n\n## Established while diagnosing (useful for whoever fixes it)\n\n- State is REMOTE: S3 `rebar-tfstate-896586841071`, key `rebar/prod/terraform.tfstate`,\n  us-east-1, `encrypt = true`, `use_lockfile = true` (no DynamoDB table).\n- `terraform init` SUCCEEDS and providers resolve; local CLI 1.15.8 clears the `>= 1.10` floor\n  that `use_lockfile` silently requires. So the break is purely the template evaluation.\n- When fixed, the change plans as an IN-PLACE update: `user_data_replace_on_change` defaults to\n  `false`, so correcting the comments does NOT rebuild the Gerrit box. Worth stating, because\n  'terraform wants to change user_data' reads alarming otherwise.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `terraform plan` runs to completion against `infra/terraform`.\n- [ ] The three comment sites escape BOTH halves (`$$`), or the comments are reworded to avoid\n      the sequence entirely.\n- [ ] A guard rejects an unescaped `${` in any file consumed by `templatefile()`, so a future\n      comment cannot silently break every terraform operation again. ShellCheck cannot catch this\n      — the file is valid bash; the breakage is in a different consumer.\n- [ ] LIVE VALIDATION — REQUIRED TO CLOSE: `terraform plan` completes AND **`terraform apply`\n      has been RUN SUCCESSFULLY** against `infra/terraform`, with the real output recorded in a\n      ticket comment. A passing plan is NOT sufficient — the operator's requirement is that\n      terraform is actually APPLIED, which is also what proves the remote-state path works end\n      to end and not merely the template evaluation.\n- [ ] Before applying, the plan is REVIEWED and recorded: the three `import` blocks for\n      `/rebar/prod/jira-url`, `/rebar/prod/jira-user` and `/rebar/prod/jira-api-token` must ADOPT\n      the operator-seeded parameters. If the plan shows any of them DESTROYED, RECREATED, or\n      having its value overwritten, STOP — those hold live credentials.\n- [ ] The apply's blast radius is stated: if it proposes changes beyond the four SSM parameters\n      and the `user_data` in-place update, that is called out before proceeding.\n\n## Note\n\nThe agent that found this deliberately did NOT edit `user_data.sh` to unblock itself: it is an\nunrelated file that feeds production `user_data`, and it belongs in its own reviewed change.\nThat was the right call.\n---\n\n## Fix plan (added by the agent working this ticket)\n\n### Confirmed mechanism\n\n`templatefile()` interpolates the WHOLE file as an HCL template; `#` is not a comment to it.\n`main.tf:63` declares exactly one template variable, `data_volume_id`. An escape-aware scan of\n`user_data.sh` (consuming `$$`/`%%` as escapes rather than naive-grepping `${`) finds 7 unescaped\ninterpolation sequences:\n\n- **4 legitimate** — `:25`, `:28`, `:53`, `:56`, all referencing the declared `data_volume_id`.\n  These MUST stay unescaped; they are the feature.\n- **3 broken** — `:92:14`, `:92:30`, `:111:46`, all referencing `PARAMS`, a *bash* associative\n  array that is not a template variable. Terraform parses `!PARAMS[@]` as HCL and rejects the `!`.\n\nIsolating the template evaluation in a scratch project proved this necessary and sufficient:\nescaping only those 3 sites renders the file completely, with all 4 `data_volume_id` sites left\nuntouched. That is also the reason the guard below must be declared-variable-aware rather than a\nblanket ban on `${`.\n\nOrigin: `fe4e-54a5-3c3a-4901` (commit `ef1a7e66a65d`), linked `caused_by`. Line 90 predates it and\nis correctly escaped, so the carrier walk stops there; the date test confirms regression rather\nthan an inherited unmet obligation.\n\n### Changes\n\n1. **`infra/terraform/user_data.sh`** — reword the three comment sites so no unescaped `${`\n   remains AND the explanation survives. Plain `$$`-escaping of the second half is rejected on\n   merit: it makes both halves render identically, so the file that actually lands on the box\n   reads \"X reduces to X\". The comments instead state the escaping RULE and the trap that caused\n   this bug, which is strictly more useful than reprinting the post-render form.\n\n2. **`scripts/check_templatefile_escapes.py`** (new) — the regression guard. ShellCheck provably\n   cannot catch this class: the file is valid bash and the breakage is in a different consumer.\n   The guard parses `templatefile(...)` call sites out of the `.tf` files, extracts each call's\n   declared variable names, escape-aware-scans the referenced template, and fails on any\n   interpolation whose root identifier is not declared. Terraform-native functions (`jsonencode`,\n   etc.) are recognised so the existing `config.js.tftpl` stays green.\n\n3. **`Makefile`** — wire into `lint`, following the established `scripts/check_*.py` pattern used\n   by the comment-hygiene, raw-git-write and ShellCheck gates.\n\n4. **`tests/unit/test_check_templatefile_escapes.py`** — RED/GREEN/mutation coverage plus the\n   `make lint` wiring assertion the sibling gates carry.\n\n### Blast radius\n\nLocal. `user_data_replace_on_change` defaults to `false`, so the comment edit plans as an\nIN-PLACE `user_data` update and does NOT rebuild the Gerrit instance. No caller depends on the\ncomment text. The guard is additive and runs static-only.\n\n### Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] `terraform plan` completes against `infra/terraform`.\n- [ ] All 3 broken sites fixed; all 4 legitimate `data_volume_id` sites left intact.\n- [ ] Guard observed RED on the broken file, GREEN after the fix, and RED again under a\n      re-introduced unescaped sequence (mutation check).\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, module-size gate and the touched suites pass.\n- [ ] `terraform apply` run, import blocks shown ADOPTING the seeded SSM parameters (no destroy,\n      recreate or value overwrite), and the real output recorded on the ticket.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/terraform/user_data.sh","reason":"The defect itself: reword the three comment sites so no unescaped ${ remains while the explanation survives."},{"path":"scripts/check_templatefile_escapes.py","reason":"New regression guard: declared-variable-aware escape check over every file consumed by templatefile()."},{"path":"Makefile","reason":"Wire the new guard into the lint target, following the existing scripts/check_*.py gate pattern."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_check_templatefile_escapes.py","reason":"RED/GREEN/mutation coverage for the guard plus the make lint wiring assertion."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"4bb6799c-eb95-4b61-ad86-722956cee692","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["terraform","infra","blocker","iac"],"ticket_id":"dd30-f10d-69f3-4c36","ticket_type":"bug","title":"terraform plan/apply is BROKEN on main: unescaped ${...} in user_data.sh comments breaks templatefile()","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["90fbc7fe-600e-4a48-843a-812d90459e40","6bafa874-2df5-4364-9447-07bf7b81cf3b","4bb6799c-eb95-4b61-ad86-722956cee692","c642b9a0-6dd5-43b3-abef-7c8a7e3e7cc5","fb7ed8d1-dd42-46d1-b41f-08c9320dffd8","75bd17cd-cd99-4a59-a412-010e6a26e967","61042ec2-bb89-426c-a84f-78f02d5bfce7","900e372a-18cb-4b08-b7ed-82d45ce3f09f"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787876733633177001,"uuid":"969d8538-59c8-458d-9bc2-5d177cbdb360"}